## Questions I Still Have

* Could bidirectional attention ideas be useful in Physical AI or robotics where perception naturally observes the whole environment at once?
* Why was Next Sentence Prediction chosen instead of another pretraining objective like summarization or compression?
* Why were Question Answering pairs used during fine-tuning instead of another format?
* How did later papers (such as RoBERTa and T5) improve upon BERT's pretraining objectives?
* How do modern frontier models combine encoder-style understanding with decoder-style generation?

---

## Observations

* GPT and BERT are built from nearly the same Transformer components, but changing the attention mask and training objective completely changes the model's behavior.
* BERT focuses on understanding language, while GPT focuses on generating language.
* Reading this paper made me realize that many future papers simply modify one part of the Transformer architecture rather than inventing an entirely new model.
* This paper also showed the beginning of scaling experiments, which would later become a major focus in GPT-2, GPT-3, and modern frontier models.

